NOTE:
A DMZ or demilitarized zone is a perimeter network that protects and adds an extra layer of security to an organization’s internal local-area network from 
untrusted traffic. The end goal of a demilitarized zone network is to allow an organization to access untrusted networks, such as the internet, while ensuring 
its private network or LAN remains secure

